From b2f271baccb480d0dc7ccdd176735d558950e496 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SovereignOS Build <build@sovereignos.local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:36:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] airpods: add BluetoothDevice#setAirPodsAlias behind
 MANAGE_AIRPODS_IDENTITY

BluetoothDevice#setAlias needs BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED or a companion device
association, so the AirPods app could rename the pair but not the phone's
own name for it (the Name row kept the old value). Add a narrow setter
instead, in the pattern of setAirPodsMetadata: only for a device that is
bonded and registered through setAirPodsIdentity, only for a name of 1 to 32
UTF-8 bytes of visible text (the rule of the app's own validation), on the
registry lock the metadata setter already uses, behind the signature or
privileged permission MANAGE_AIRPODS_IDENTITY. It changes no other device
property.

airpods: refuse an alias that ends in a no-break space or draws nothing

String.strip() leaves a no-break space in place, and the Hangul fillers and the Braille blank are letters or symbols, so the alias policy accepted names that look empty. Same rule as AapCodec.isValidName in the AirPods app.
